      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSuperbly positioned in the heart of Curraghbinny, this exceptional detached bungalow enjoys a wonderful, elevated setting on approximately 0.35 acres, with a coveted southerly aspect and truly breathtaking views. From its commanding position, the property looks across a large green area towards Cork Harbour, the Royal Cork Yacht Club, Crosshaven Village and the surrounding countryside, creating an ever-changing coastal panorama.\nThe house is approached through attractive arches which lead into a bright and spacious entrance hallway, immediately setting the tone for the generous and light-filled accommodation beyond. A particular feature of this home is the wealth of reception and entertaining space, with many of the principal rooms positioned to take full advantage of the spectacular outlook.\nAt the heart of the home is the bright kitchen/dining room, a wonderfully inviting space with double doors opening directly onto a terrace overlooking the harbour and surrounding coastline. Just off the kitchen is a large dining area, ideal for entertaining family and friends, with two sets of double doors framing the views and opening onto a further terrace to the front.\nThe formal reception room is an elegant and comfortable space featuring a gas fire, a striking wall of windows and double doors, allowing natural light to flood the room while capturing the magnificent views beyond. Also overlooking the front is a more relaxed living room, offering excellent flexibility and equally suitable for use as an additional bedroom if required. To the rear of the property is a charming lounge which would make an ideal home office, study or quiet retreat.\nThe bedroom accommodation is equally well considered. The generous master bedroom benefits from a walk-in wardrobe and en suite bathroom, providing a private and comfortable sanctuary. A further bedroom to the rear also enjoys its own en suite, making it ideal for family members or visiting guests.\nOutside, the elevated grounds and terraces provide wonderful opportunities for outdoor dining, entertaining and relaxation while enjoying the exceptional southerly aspect and captivating harbour views. The setting offers a rare sense of peace and space, while remaining remarkably convenient to nearby amenities.\nFor those who enjoy the outdoors, Curraghbinny Woods and the waterfront are close at hand, offering beautiful surroundings for walking, swimming and enjoying the natural landscape. Boating enthusiasts are particularly well catered for, with Crosshaven just a five-minute trip by water or, for the more adventurous, a swim across the harbour.\nDespite its tranquil coastal setting, Curraghbinny is exceptionally accessible. Carrigaline is approximately 10 minutes away, Douglas 20 minutes, while Cork City and Cork Airport can both be reached in approximately 30 minutes."
      },
